# STRESS 06b — TEXT FLOW
#
# Alignment, vertical alignment, wrapping, leading and justification.
#
# Line breaking is greedy, not Knuth-Plass (DESIGN.md section 6): the wrapper
# takes as many words as fit and moves on. That produces a raggier right edge
# than a paragraph optimiser would, and in exchange the output never moves
# because somebody tuned a penalty constant — which is what makes a golden file
# worth having.
#
# Justification spreads the word gaps of every line but the last, through the
# same DistributeTicks that splits a column, so a justified line ends exactly
# on the measure.

page
  size: letter
  margin: 0.5in

defaults
  font: IBM Plex Sans
  font-size: 8pt
  color: gray(0.12)

section
  height: 28pt
  text "06b · TEXT FLOW"
    font: IBM Plex Mono
    font-size: 14pt
    font-weight: bold
    tracking: 1.2pt

section
  height: 22pt
  text "align, on the same paragraph in four boxes of the same width."
    font-size: 7.5pt
    color: gray(0.45)

section
  height: 116pt
  gap: 8pt
  column
    width: fill
    box
      height: 100pt
      border-width: 0.4pt
      border-color: gray(0.6)
      padding: 6pt
      text "Greedy line breaking, not Knuth-Plass: the wrapper takes as many words as fit and moves on, so output never shifts."
        font-size: 7.5pt
        align: left
    text "align: left"
      font-size: 5.5pt
      color: gray(0.4)
      padding-top: 3pt
  column
    width: fill
    box
      height: 100pt
      border-width: 0.4pt
      border-color: gray(0.6)
      padding: 6pt
      text "Greedy line breaking, not Knuth-Plass: the wrapper takes as many words as fit and moves on, so output never shifts."
        font-size: 7.5pt
        align: center
    text "align: center"
      font-size: 5.5pt
      color: gray(0.4)
      padding-top: 3pt
  column
    width: fill
    box
      height: 100pt
      border-width: 0.4pt
      border-color: gray(0.6)
      padding: 6pt
      text "Greedy line breaking, not Knuth-Plass: the wrapper takes as many words as fit and moves on, so output never shifts."
        font-size: 7.5pt
        align: right
    text "align: right"
      font-size: 5.5pt
      color: gray(0.4)
      padding-top: 3pt
  column
    width: fill
    box
      height: 100pt
      border-width: 0.4pt
      border-color: gray(0.6)
      padding: 6pt
      text "Greedy line breaking, not Knuth-Plass: the wrapper takes as many words as fit and moves on, so output never shifts."
        font-size: 7.5pt
        align: justify
    text "align: justify"
      font-size: 5.5pt
      color: gray(0.4)
      padding-top: 3pt

section
  height: 26pt
  valign: bottom
  text "valign, with one short line in a box far taller than it needs. `baseline` puts the first baseline where `top` would have put it, which is what keeps two adjacent boxes' first lines level when their type sizes differ."
    font-size: 7.5pt
    color: gray(0.45)

section
  height: 90pt
  gap: 8pt
  column
    width: fill
    box
      height: 74pt
      border-width: 0.4pt
      border-color: gray(0.6)
      padding: 6pt
      valign: top
      text "valign: top"
        font-size: 8pt
  column
    width: fill
    box
      height: 74pt
      border-width: 0.4pt
      border-color: gray(0.6)
      padding: 6pt
      valign: middle
      text "valign: middle"
        font-size: 8pt
  column
    width: fill
    box
      height: 74pt
      border-width: 0.4pt
      border-color: gray(0.6)
      padding: 6pt
      valign: bottom
      text "valign: bottom"
        font-size: 8pt
  column
    width: fill
    box
      height: 74pt
      border-width: 0.4pt
      border-color: gray(0.6)
      padding: 6pt
      valign: baseline
      text "valign: baseline"
        font-size: 8pt

section
  height: 26pt
  valign: bottom
  text "line-height is text leading as a multiple of font-size. It is NOT the ruled-line spacing — that is line-pitch, and setting line-height on a ruled panel warns (W030) because it is the trap the two names create."
    font-size: 7.5pt
    color: gray(0.45)

section
  height: 116pt
  gap: 8pt
  column
    width: fill
    box
      height: 100pt
      border-width: 0.4pt
      border-color: gray(0.6)
      padding: 6pt
      text "Greedy line breaking, not Knuth-Plass: the wrapper takes as many words as fit and moves on, so output never shifts."
        font-size: 7.5pt
        line-height: 1.0
    text "line-height: 1.0"
      font-size: 5.5pt
      color: gray(0.4)
      padding-top: 3pt
  column
    width: fill
    box
      height: 100pt
      border-width: 0.4pt
      border-color: gray(0.6)
      padding: 6pt
      text "Greedy line breaking, not Knuth-Plass: the wrapper takes as many words as fit and moves on, so output never shifts."
        font-size: 7.5pt
        line-height: 1.2
    text "line-height: 1.2"
      font-size: 5.5pt
      color: gray(0.4)
      padding-top: 3pt
  column
    width: fill
    box
      height: 100pt
      border-width: 0.4pt
      border-color: gray(0.6)
      padding: 6pt
      text "Greedy line breaking, not Knuth-Plass: the wrapper takes as many words as fit and moves on, so output never shifts."
        font-size: 7.5pt
        line-height: 1.35
    text "line-height: 1.35"
      font-size: 5.5pt
      color: gray(0.4)
      padding-top: 3pt
  column
    width: fill
    box
      height: 100pt
      border-width: 0.4pt
      border-color: gray(0.6)
      padding: 6pt
      text "Greedy line breaking, not Knuth-Plass: the wrapper takes as many words as fit and moves on, so output never shifts."
        font-size: 7.5pt
        line-height: 1.8
    text "line-height: 1.8"
      font-size: 5.5pt
      color: gray(0.4)
      padding-top: 3pt

section
  height: 26pt
  valign: bottom
  text "wrap: false keeps a run on one line whatever the measure. Note that the box's `overflow: clip` does not clip it — clipping is applied to decorations, not to text — so this is how type ends up outside its box."
    font-size: 7.5pt
    color: gray(0.45)

section
  height: 56pt
  gap: 8pt
  column
    width: fill
    box
      height: 44pt
      border-width: 0.4pt
      border-color: gray(0.6)
      padding: 5pt
      text "wrap: true — this sentence is longer than the box and folds onto a second line."
        font-size: 7.5pt
        wrap: true
  column
    width: fill
    box
      height: 44pt
      border-width: 0.4pt
      border-color: gray(0.6)
      padding: 5pt
      overflow: clip
      text "wrap: false — longer than its box, one line, spilling right"
        font-size: 7.5pt
        wrap: false
  column
    width: fill

section
  height: 26pt
  valign: bottom
  text "numeric-style is in the property table with a `tabular` default, and nothing reads it: the figures below are identical. IBM Plex's default figures are already tabular in Mono, so a planner's columns of digits line up regardless."
    font-size: 7.5pt
    color: gray(0.45)

section
  height: 60pt
  gap: 8pt
  column
    width: fill
    box
      height: 48pt
      border-width: 0.4pt
      border-color: gray(0.6)
      padding: 5pt
      text "1111111111"
        font: IBM Plex Mono
        font-size: 9pt
        numeric-style: tabular
      text "0000000000"
        font: IBM Plex Mono
        font-size: 9pt
        numeric-style: tabular
      text "numeric-style: tabular"
        font-size: 5.5pt
        color: gray(0.4)
  column
    width: fill
    box
      height: 48pt
      border-width: 0.4pt
      border-color: gray(0.6)
      padding: 5pt
      text "1111111111"
        font: IBM Plex Mono
        font-size: 9pt
        numeric-style: proportional
      text "0000000000"
        font: IBM Plex Mono
        font-size: 9pt
        numeric-style: proportional
      text "numeric-style: proportional"
        font-size: 5.5pt
        color: gray(0.4)
  column
    width: fill(2)

section
  height: 26pt
  valign: bottom
  text "Text inside a decorated box flows normally: it does not snap to the writing rules. The decoration computes its baselines and the painter does not use them, so a line of type and the rule under it are independent."
    font-size: 7.5pt
    color: gray(0.45)

section
  height: 96pt
  gap: 8pt
  column
    width: fill
    box
      height: 82pt
      border-width: 0.4pt
      border-color: gray(0.6)
      padding: 6pt
      line-style: ruled
      line-pitch: 6mm
      line-color: gray(0.82)
      text "Three lines of type in a 6mm ruled box at the default 1.35 leading. The type and the rules are on different rhythms."
        font-size: 7.5pt
    text "line-pitch 6mm, line-height 1.35"
      font-size: 5.5pt
      color: gray(0.4)
      padding-top: 3pt
  column
    width: fill
    box
      height: 82pt
      border-width: 0.4pt
      border-color: gray(0.6)
      padding: 6pt
      line-style: ruled
      line-pitch: 6mm
      line-color: gray(0.82)
      baseline-on-rule: false
      text "The same box with baseline-on-rule off. Nothing moves, because nothing in the painter reads a decoration's baselines yet."
        font-size: 7.5pt
    text "baseline-on-rule: false"
      font-size: 5.5pt
      color: gray(0.4)
      padding-top: 3pt
  column
    width: fill
    box
      height: 82pt
      border-width: 0.4pt
      border-color: gray(0.6)
      padding: 6pt
      line-style: ruled
      line-color: gray(0.82)
      line-pitch: 13.7pt
      text "Set line-pitch to the type's own leading — 7.5pt at 1.35 is 10.125pt, and 13.7pt here — and the two rhythms agree by construction rather than by luck."
        font-size: 7.5pt
    text "line-pitch tuned by hand"
      font-size: 5.5pt
      color: gray(0.4)
      padding-top: 3pt
  column
    width: fill

section
  height: auto
  valign: bottom
  text "auto-shrink is not on this sheet: it only acts when text does not fit. Sheet 09 carries the deliberate warnings."
    font-size: 6.5pt
    color: gray(0.5)
